# vit_v1_endpoint: ViT transfer of the BERT endpoint s3_embed_chunk, measured 2026-09-29 as
# vit_v1_endpoint_r3 (limb loop, per-layer driver, embedding chunks; no spill, no defer).
#
# port       lever set byte-identical to s3_embed_chunk; driver changes forced by the model only:
#              no attention mask      mask tensor, its encryption and sub-graph removed: 14 sub-graphs
#                                     (BERT driver: 15)
#              no pooler              head = final LayerNorm + CLS slice
#              patch embedding        one pixel_values operand instead of two token tensors
#              local checkpoint dir   image carries only BERT, nodes offline
# phase B    pair = vit_v1_endpoint vs vit_v0_default. The BERT mask sub-graph difference (524,288 B,
#            one round; reason for s5_per_layer's transcript_artefact) cannot occur here.
# inert      SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16 drives embed_chunk_gpu (vocabulary one-hot matmul); ViT has no
#            vocabulary, so the lever is inert; kept so the set stays unchanged (as SHAFT-CPU-ViT).
#            Not covered by check_lever. SHAFT_LIMB_LOOP=1 is guarded and announces (MatMul.forward).

BASELINE_SCRIPT=$BASE/vit_perlayer_gpu.py
SHAFT_SCRIPT=vit_perlayer_gpu.py
SHAFT_LIMB_LOOP=1
SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_MODEL=/vit SHAFT_MAX_LENGTH=197"

# impl_snapshot: vit_perlayer_gpu.py
# Driver plus lever modules, named in shaft-gpu/impl/stepenv/vit_v1_endpoint_r3.env; snapshot because
# the module set is given in full per step. Artifacts under systems/shaft-gpu/impl/ (parent's image).
# pool_attacked: host
# cost_class: free
#
# evidence: equivalent
# plaintext_equivalence: impl/equiv_per_layer_vit.py
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pool       at vit_v0_default's peak: W_host 160.79 (peak 2,963,720 kB), W_vram 106.78 (1,968,128 kB);
#            rule 3 -> host (as s5_per_layer on BERT). Outcome: device falls 3.151x, host 1.442x.
# cost       free, measured; corrected walls, medians n=3:
#              vit_v0_default   40.5 s
#              vit_v1_endpoint  35.7 s      -11.9%
#            (PUMA s1_weight_stream -10.6%, BERT s5_per_layer -2.2%: small repeated traces.)
# phase B    (a) transcript: 19,769,912,480 B / 1,468 rounds in v0 and v1, all six runs; no
#                transcript_artefact needed (no mask sub-graph in ViT).
#            (b) plaintext equivalence re-run in this image (same decomposition: embeddings, 12
#                ViTLayer, LayerNorm then classifier on CLS).
# check      baseline transcript equals SHAFT-CPU-ViT's to the byte (19,769,912,480 / 1,468).
